From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:26:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Carry coreboot's TPM 2.0 measurements into
 Tcg2Dxe

With measured boot, coreboot extends the PCRs of a TPM 2.0 with what it
loads and logs each measurement in its own crypto agile event log, which
it publishes as the log area of the ACPI TPM2 table. An OS booted through
UEFI reads the log of EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL instead (Linux takes the one of
the EFI configuration table), and Tcg2Dxe starts that log afresh: the
events of coreboot are missing, and the log no longer replays to PCR 0
and 2, which hold coreboot's measurements.

Tcg2Dxe already takes the events of the firmware phases before it, as
gTcgEvent2EntryHobGuid HOBs that it logs without extending again. In
UefiPayloadEntry, find the TPM2 table among the bootloader's ACPI tables,
read the spec ID event at its log area for the digest sizes, and build
one such HOB for each event, up to the first with no digest (coreboot
clears the rest of the area) or the end of the area. Tcg2Dxe drops the
digests of banks that are not active; with a bank active for which the
events have no digest it says so, as for any PEI event.

Nothing changes without a TPM2 table, or with one whose log area does
not start with a "Spec ID Event03" (a TPM 1.2 log, or none).

TEST=gcc -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wextra -Werror of Tcg2EventLog.c with the
EDK2 headers, debug and MDEPKG_NDEBUG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
